{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310610,"nonce":"WBXvvcM5J396Sa1rWYlKObeuGtA=","title":"HIGH-IMPACT compiler bug: conditionally reassigning a Float local (esp. loop-carried) emits a heap box (haxe_box_float_ptr) per update ...","message":"MIR shows the mechanism exactly: a Float that merges at a control-flow join\nbecomes a phi, and the PHI IS BOXED even though it is typed f64.\n\n    bb4:\n      $54 = phi f64 [bb3: $48]\n      $56 = phi f64 [bb3: $52]\n      $59 = call haxe_box_float_ptr($56)    \u003c- boxed phi\n\nSource shape (nue/nue/Int8Matmul.hx, quantizeActRow — runs PER ROW, PER MATMUL,\nPER TOKEN, so this is the dominant allocator):\n\n    var maxAbs = mAcc.get(0);\n    var l1 = mAcc.get(1); if (l1 \u003e maxAbs) maxAbs = l1;   // x3\n\nCall sites with Float box calls, from the MIR of a real llama-chat bundle\n(legend-resolved; a raw grep finds NOTHING because MIR prints `call fnN(...)`):\n  26 nue.sampling.GenerationLoop.generate · 10 Q4Matmul.dumpDecodeSplit (cold)\n   6 Int8Matmul.quantizeActRow · 6 Int8Matmul.quantizeWeight\n   6 GQAttention.dumpAttnProfile · 2 FlashDecode.bandOneSigned/bandOneShifted\n   2 SpinPool.workerLoop\nMeasured 1,876,152 haxe_box_float_ptr calls / 57 MB in one run, NEVER FREED\n(haxe_box_* is invisible to insert_free.rs — see\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]]).\n\nNOT reproducible in isolation: `if (c) f = f + 1.5`, `if (c) f = Sys.time()` and\nthe ternary form all emit ZERO boxes in a small test. The trigger needs the\nlarger function context, so reduce from quantizeActRow, do not start from a toy.\n\n`malloc_history` renders JIT frames as `??? (in \u003cunknown binary\u003e) [0xADDR]`.\nMatch ADDR against `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` output (name -\u003e address, nearest\nstart \u003c= addr). **Check the delta**: a +109880 byte delta \"matched\" the wrong\nfunction and sent me down a dead end; +360 is real. The LLVM backend did not\ndump pointers at all until 2026-08-10 (only 640 of ~1638 functions were\ncovered) — now instrumented in llvm_jit_backend.rs at both the lazy and bulk\naddress-resolution paths, giving 1018.\n**Caveat: LLVM inlines the pool work into SpinPool.workerLoop**, so an address\ninside workerLoop may belong to whatever band closure was inlined there. Confirm\nagainst the MIR before believing an attribution.\n\n\nPure-Haxe matmul (RAYZOR_HAXE_MATMUL) RSS climbed to 3-4GB on long contexts vs FFI's flat ~1.5GB.\nNOT the KV cache (Q8, small), NOT flash (matmul-only reproduced it), NOT InsertFreePass tensors.\n\n1. `vmmap -summary \u003cpid\u003e`: DefaultMallocZone COUNT column = live alloc count. 30-60M live 16-byte\n   objects with climbing count = per-element leak. (16 bytes = boxed f64: tag+payload.)\n2. `heap \u003cpid\u003e` (SIGSTOP the process first so it scans clean): size histogram — `16[29487523]`\n   pinned it to 29.5M 16-byte objects.\n3. `MallocStackLogging=1 \u003ccmd\u003e` + `malloc_history \u003cpid\u003e -callTree`: named the allocator —\n   `haxe_box_float_ptr`, called from `??? (in \u003cunknown binary\u003e)` = JIT code.\n4. `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` in the SAME run → map the JIT caller addr to a function by range\n   (matmul/runBanded/matmulFused/lambda). Then lldb `disassemble --start-address \u003cfn\u003e`: the box\n   is `fmov d0, dN; blr xK; fmov d0, dN` (float to arg reg, call, RESULT DISCARDED).\n\n- `if (a \u003c 0) a = -a;` — reassigning the loaded Float in an if boxes it per negative element.\n- `if (aa \u003e maxAbs) maxAbs = aa;` — reassigning the LOOP-CARRIED maxAbs boxes per update.\n- `Math.floor(v+0.5)` / `Math.ceil(v-0.5)` — boxes the Float ARGUMENT per call.\nCommon thread: a Float that is (a) conditionally reassigned, and/or (b) loop-carried/escaping,\ngets a heap box instead of staying in an fp register. Same family as the stealLoop Int-\u003eFloat\ndecay (c33c25ab) and the f16-carry decay (13dff852).\n\n- abs: `var na = -a; var aa = a \u003e na ? a : na;` (ternary → fcsel, no box). NOT `if (a\u003c0) a=-a`.\n- max-reduce: `maxAbs = aa \u003e maxAbs ? aa : maxAbs;` (unconditional select → fcsel). NOT\n  `if (aa \u003e maxAbs) maxAbs = aa`.\n- round-half-away: `v \u003e= 0 ? Std.int(v+0.5) : Std.int(v-0.5)` (Std.int = fptosi intrinsic, no\n  box). NOT Math.floor/ceil (those box the arg).\nApplied in Q4Matmul.quantizeBlock, FlashDecode.decode q-quantize, Q8Cache.quantBlock.\n\n30M live 16-byte allocs → ~0. Total allocs 9.85M → 5.44M. 4000-tok RSS FLAT ~1.5GB (was\nclimbing past 2.7GB toward 4GB), matches FFI. Throughput ALSO up ~50→72 tok/s (hot-path allocs\ngone). argmax 33/33 vs FFI, suite 159/159.\n\nThe MIR/codegen path that boxes a conditionally-reassigned / loop-carried Float should keep it\nin an fp register (fcsel/phi), never `haxe_box_float_ptr`. Ternary already lowers correctly\n(fcsel) — the bug is specifically the `if (cond) floatvar = ...` reassignment and Math.floor/ceil\narg passing. Fix generally so kernels needn't hand-avoid `if`-reassign of Floats. See also\n[[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]] (the other same-session compiler-bug cluster).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_float_conditional_reassign_boxes` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}